{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043682-when-does-a-human-fetus-get-a-soul-in-the-cod","id":1043682,"title":"When does a human fetus get a soul in the CoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T12:39:55-08:00","id":1043682,"title":"When does a human fetus get a soul in the CoD?","content":"Is it third trimester, after it's born and becomes a baby, or conception. <br /> <br /> I ask because it occurs to me that a female Treme Lich could get pregnate, steal the fetus' soul or keep herself from giving birth till it has a soul, then take the soul and have a miscarriage, and no one would be the wiser, especially if she hides she's pregnate using magic.<br /> <br /> Just a weird thought that came me. I guess with the right life spells a male Treme could it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:45:55-08:00","id":1043684,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say birth, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:54:17-08:00","id":1043691,"title":"","content":"Just go with the old Hebrew and Greek traditions; the soul enters the body at the first breath. It gives a nice, easy dividing line and prevents abortion debates at the game table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:21:15-08:00","id":1043704,"title":"","content":"I think Dave said that humans get souls when they gain a sense of self. Or was it a Name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:31:52-08:00","id":1043707,"title":"","content":"Gaining a sense of self is when the Lie sets in, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:55:34-08:00","id":1043716,"title":"","content":"Arguably, it happens at conception, citing the baby from the Lovers card in KttST who Awakened immediately upon being conceived. That's obviously also a special case though, so...what's most appropriate for your story would be my answer.<br /> <br /> Assuming for a second it does happen at conception though: Going with the Tremere thing, eventually they need to consume souls at least once a month and there isn't ever a mention of baby-farming. If the soul arrived on conception I assume that said Tremere could wreck the soul economy with how quickly she could cycle through conception, stealing the soul, miscarrying, and getting pregnant again. There might just be a taboo on Tremere having kids though to cut down on the overall number of souls (All the souls) that they have to collect. Also, it's pretty unlikely they'd be caught (Which is kind of the point in a narrative structure). If they do get caught though, that's some pretty good subtle sinisterly behavior.<br /> <br /> On baby's first breath means it would be an inefficient method of gathering souls, but you're guaranteed one month of survival a year at least. Higher risk of being caught too. It also raises the question of why the Tremere wouldn't just hang out around hospital nurseries and grab all the infant souls at once on a globe spanning hospital hopping spree. More obvious and likely to be caught and very overtly sinister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T15:45:32-08:00","id":1043756,"title":"","content":"There's no way anyone from OPP or WW will ever directly answer that question, and I don't blame them. It's far too fraught with political implications, even for the notably liberal companies.<br /> <br /> Simply decide what's best for your chronicle.<br /> <br /> My own headcanon states that a baby shares a soul with the mother until shortly after birth when the baby's shared soul shard slowly develops independence as the child also develops a sense of self.<br /> <br /> This allows a little bit of compromise as a fetus doesn't have it's own unique soul, but killing it still potentially damages the mother's soul. This would be consistent with mages who creates soul stone (and might have some &quot;interesting&quot; potential for bad or deranged mage parents). YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:38:38-08:00","id":1043779,"title":"","content":"That would have weird implications with a Tremere mother with her anti-soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:28:57-08:00","id":1043815,"title":"","content":"\u2026It's pretty explicit, guys:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw2e Core, p98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The origin and destination of souls remains a Mystery even to the Awakened \u2014 they appear at birth and vanish completely at the moment of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:31:40-08:00","id":1043998,"title":"","content":"The game explicitly spells it out, yeah. You get a soul when you're born and you lose it when you die.<br /> <br /> As far as the abortion debate goes, the games also come down hard on the side of &quot;people without souls are still people&quot;, so the soul thing doesn't exactly settle that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:37:11-08:00","id":1044006,"title":"","content":"For a Tremere, an retirement home, hospital or hospice might be a better option. Old people are expected to die and the moment of death for those sleepers can be predicted with the Death or Time Arcana. Giving only a short time for the victim to be discovered missing their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:40:59-08:00","id":1044007,"title":"","content":"For some reason I thought Tremere were sterile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:09:14-08:00","id":1044516,"title":"","content":"I could see this question becoming the basis for an interesting Obsession: a Moros studying pregnancy in order to explore the origin of souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:52:36-08:00","id":1045037,"title":"","content":"That's what my Moros did in a game, and I am probably going to explore the idea more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:50:09-08:00","id":1045318,"title":"","content":"One way to explore this from a mechanical stanpoint is to see what a Soul does in the game. <br /> Essentially, it allows you to correctly &quot;use&quot; your Virtue and Vice, enter your Oneiros, suffer Integrity loss normally, etc. <br /> So, one could test any of those things at different human developmental stages with magic, an interesting Mystery. <br /> <br /> Another interesting point: Would even a new born baby have a Virtue, Vice, Oneiros, Integrity, etc? Or do those things form over their early years? Maybe the Soul kind of accrues over time as you develop it, and getting your sense of self (which triggers the Curse of Quiessence) stops your soul from developing further on its own until you pull the curse away by Awakening...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:40:11-08:00","id":1045478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043682-when-does-a-human-fetus-get-a-soul-in-the-cod?p=1045318#post1045318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to explore this from a mechanical stanpoint is to see what a Soul does in the game.<br /> Essentially, it allows you to correctly &quot;use&quot; your Virtue and Vice, enter your Oneiros, suffer Integrity loss normally, etc.<br /> So, one could test any of those things at different human developmental stages with magic, an interesting Mystery.<br /> <br /> Another interesting point: Would even a new born baby have a Virtue, Vice, Oneiros, Integrity, etc? Or do those things form over their early years? Maybe the Soul kind of accrues over time as you develop it, and getting your sense of self (which triggers the Curse of Quiessence) stops your soul from developing further on its own until you pull the curse away by Awakening...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And now I picture the local consilium being busy guarding the hospitals and orphanages from Reaper invasions. Or busy hoarding it for their own studies. Probably both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:32:29-08:00","id":1045778,"title":"","content":"A cabal organizes a controversial &quot;soul transplant&quot; program, taking souls from terminal patients and sending them (no questions asked) to areas hit by Reaper activity or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:57:08-08:00","id":1045800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043682-when-does-a-human-fetus-get-a-soul-in-the-cod?p=1045318#post1045318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would even a new born baby have a Virtue, Vice, Oneiros, Integrity, etc? </div> </div> </div> </div>Newborns don't even have object permanence. I don't imagine they're capable of moral judgements.<br /> <br /> That said, they can develop developmental and psychological problems, so they might have Integrity.<br /> <br /> As an aside, let me take a moment to say that the Ferber method is fucking awful. If your baby is crying, pick it the fuck up. Leaving them to cry leaves them with an anxious attachment style. Evolution did what it did for a reason.<br /> <br /> Don't mind me, this is just a hot button with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}